WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.860
- [Ray] Principles for Success.

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.100
An Ultra Mini-Series Adventure

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.430
in 30 Minutes and in Eight Episodes.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:10.373
Episode Eight- Struggle Well.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.240
So far, I described how I learned

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.150
to confront my own realities, my problems,

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:18.220
my mistakes and weaknesses,

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.800
and how I surrounded myself with others

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.700
who could do things better than I could.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.530
This was the most
effective way I discovered

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:28.308
for making great decisions.

00:00:28.308 --> 00:00:29.141
(cheering)

00:00:29.141 --> 00:00:31.330
This is not the normal way of being

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:34.720
but through this approach,
I became very successful.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.880
And being successful enabled me

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.621
to meet extraordinarily successful people

00:00:39.621 --> 00:00:41.890
and see how they think.

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:45.220
I've discovered that their
journeys were similar to mine.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.810
You might not know it
but they all struggle

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.090
and they all have weaknesses.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.860
That they all get around
by working with people

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:57.220
who see risks and opportunities
that they would miss.

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.480
Over time, I learned that by nature

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.430
most people's greatest
strengths are also connected

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:05.110
to their most significant weaknesses.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:07.700
And striving hard for big things is bound

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.150
to lead you to painful falls.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.750
It's just part of the process.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.070
Such setbacks will test you.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:17.160
They sort people.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:20.411
Some think hard about what
caused their setbacks,

00:01:20.411 --> 00:01:23.510
learned lessons, and continue progressing

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:24.900
toward their goals.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:28.030
While others decide that
this game is not for them

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:29.423
and get off the field,

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.220
I've come to realize that success

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:35.287
is not a matter of attaining one's goals.

00:01:35.287 --> 00:01:37.320
I found that when I reached

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.880
each new higher level of success,

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:41.563
I really remained satisfied.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.050
The things we're striving
for are just the bait.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:49.370
Struggling to get them
forces us to evolve.

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:50.890
And it is this struggle

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:55.370
to our personal evolution with
others that is the reward.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:58.020
I no longer wanted to
get across the jungle

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.120
but instead wanted to find greater

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.630
and greater challenges to go after.

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.920
Surrounded by great
people working together

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:08.060
on a shared journey.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:10.710
Eventually, the success of the mission

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:13.510
and the well-being of
the people alongside me

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.073
became more important than my own success.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.460
I also started to see beyond myself

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:23.990
and wanted others to be successful
when I'm no longer here.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:27.230
I realized that if I failed to do that,

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.390
I will be a failure.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:31.750
I struggle with this now.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.220
We all struggle with different
things at different times

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:38.700
until we either choose to
give up or until we die

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:41.563
and become part of the
larger evolutionary story.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:46.730
This is how all machines work
and are recycled through time.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.140
When a machine breaks down,

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:50.250
it's parts go back into the system

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.520
to become parts of new machines

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.143
that also evolved through time.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.890
Sometimes this makes us sad

00:02:56.890 --> 00:03:00.130
because we become very
attached to our machines.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:02.600
But if you look at it from a higher level,

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.690
it's really beautiful to observe

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:07.480
how the machine of evolution works.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:12.480
Now you must decide for
yourself how you will evolve.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:15.100
Forget about where these
principles came from.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:18.060
Just assess whether or
not they are useful to you

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.190
and evolve them to sooth your own needs.

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:23.430
As with all of life's decisions,

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:26.900
what you do with them
is ultimately up to you.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:30.190
My only hope for you is
that you have the courage

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:33.680
to struggle and evolve
well to make your life

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.353
as great as it can be.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.360
Thank you and goodbye.

